    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The Amalfi Coast runs along the southern edge of the Sorrento Peninsula in Campania. Steep cliffs drop to the sea, and the towns of Positano, Amalfi and Atrani cling to the slopes.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Villages sit on terraces cut into the hillside, linked by stairways and the narrow SS163 coast road. Lemon groves grow on the terraces. Ravello looks down on the coast from the heights above Amalfi.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "May, June and September are the best months. Ferries and buses beat the road in summer, and sturdy shoes matter on the stairs.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
